    "body": "We’re back this year with another spooky edition of The Weekly Break Out. “Mr. Skeleton” (aka Editor-in-Chief Aaron Mehta) welcomes three special guests — and Breaking Defense’s senior networks reporter, who again appears to have not gotten the memo — to talk about what’s keeping them up at night.\nAdm. T. Hitchens joins us from Starfleet to discuss weapons in space; Scarecarley Welch is unsettled by a leadership vacuum atop the Army; Mark “Mark” Pomerleau lays out a few cyber conundrums; and Digger Rockwell explains what’s especially alarming about the Air Force’s nuclear weapons plans for the months to come.\nIf this episode wasn’t too scary for you, make sure to sign up for our newsletter to see what else we have up our sleeve. And Happy Halloween from the Breaking Defense team!\nBreaking Defense Video\npresented by\nA more flexible way to defend maneuver forces from drones that doesn’t tie them down [Sponsored]\nWatch Now »\nWhat’s haunting the Pentagon this Halloween?\nWatch Now »\npresented by\nThe new must-have capabilities for drones [Sponsored]\nWatch Now »\nArmy’s tech chief talks autonomy, acquisition and the future of drones\nWatch Now »\nDrones take over AUSA, plus the Army’s plan to bring in new vendors\nWatch Now »\nHegseth talks autonomy at AUSA, a key show focus\nWatch Now »\nArmy doubles down on autonomy, stakes out Indo-Pacific role: AUSA Day 2\nWatch Now »\nTelle talks ‘manufacturing rodeo,’ supply chain ‘weak links’: AUSA Day 1\nWatch Now »\nNew leaders, new drone command: What we expect from AUSA 2026\nWatch Now »\nUnpacking Boeing’s F/A-XX win, plus a report from wartime Ukraine\nWatch Now »\nScroll for more video",
